From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: make the user documentation optional

gnome.yelp() runs itstool to merge translations into the help pages, and
subdir('help') is unconditional, so configure stops on a build that has no
itstool:

  help/meson.build:34:6: ERROR: Program 'itstool' not found or not executable

Add a help option, defaulting to true so nothing changes for anyone building
normally, and skip the subdir when it is off.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/meson_options.txt
+++ b/meson_options.txt
@@ -27,3 +27,9 @@
   value: 'disabled',
   description: 'Enable elementary OS integration. Requires Granite'
 )
+
+option('help',
+  type: 'boolean',
+  value: true,
+  description: 'Build the user documentation with yelp (needs itstool)'
+)
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -158,7 +158,9 @@
                       language: 'c')
 
 subdir('data')
-subdir('help')
+if get_option('help')
+  subdir('help')
+endif
 subdir('po')
 subdir('third-party')
 subdir('lib')
